(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[27 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [28 1 "//"] [29 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [30 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [31 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [32 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [33 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [34 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [35 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [36 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [37 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [38 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [39 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [40 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [63 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [75 2 "// alert is the description OpenSSL would send, 0 when none: the SNI callback's (its *al; Go's server sends"] [76 2 "// internal_error when GetConfigForClient fails), a failed verification's (ssl_x509err2alert; Go sends"] [77 2 "// bad_certificate). The transport puts it in Go's alert record while that is in the clear: always for the"] [78 2 "// SNI callback (before the server's hello), under TLS 1.2 for a verification."] [105 98 "// a fatal alert in the clear"] [120 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [141 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [145 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [149 26 "// a weak reference, as _ssl's (queue 241: a dead owner fails the SNI callback)"] [165 24 "// the incoming record being fed, for the message callback"] [166 24 "// the bytes at the head of the engine's output already traced (a socket's unsent rest)"] [167 24 "// the version the message callback reports: the server hello's, once seen"] [171 22 "// 3.15.2's got_eof_error (gh-148292): an SSLEOFError raised, read, write and do_handshake raise it again"] [174 1 "// eofAgain is 3.15.2's set_eof_error: after an SSLEOFError, read, write and do_handshake raise SSLEOFError again with"] [175 1 "// no library and no reason (queue 263; 3.14.10 has no got_eof_error)."] [187 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [191 12 "// the alert OpenSSL sends for the code (ssl_x509err2alert), 0 for Go's bad_certificate"] [196 1 "// Unwrap is the alert the vendored crypto/tls sends for the failed verification (queue 552: an AlertError returned by"] [197 1 "// VerifyConnection; Go's own sends bad_certificate, which the transport could rewrite only while in the clear)."] [205 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [220 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [221 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [238 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [243 2 "// queue 552: a PSK suite only with this side's PSK callback (OpenSSL disables kPSK without one)"] [271 3 "// queue 552: SSL_VERIFY_POST_HANDSHAKE, set by newPySSLSocket only with SSL_VERIFY_PEER (bpo-37428): a TLS 1.3"] [272 3 "// client that offered post_handshake_auth is asked for its certificate by verify_client_post_handshake alone"] [292 33 "// SSL_set_post_handshake_auth (queue 552)"] [300 1 "// pskClient is psk_client_callback: the context's callback called on the Python thread with the server's identity"] [301 1 "// hint (None when absent or empty), its (identity, psk) taken as \"z#y#\"; an error unraisable, no PSK offered."] [317 12 "// an invalid UTF-8 hint drops the connection, no exception"] [345 40 "// PSK_MAX_IDENTITY_LEN + 1, PSK_MAX_PSK_LEN"] [356 1 "// pskServer is psk_server_callback: the context's callback called with the client's identity (None when empty), its"] [357 1 "// bytes the key; an error unraisable, the identity refused."] [387 1 "// autoChain is OpenSSL's automatic chain (ssl_add_cert_chain without SSL_MODE_NO_AUTO_CHAIN): a certificate"] [388 1 "// loaded without its chain is sent with the chain the context's store builds for it, as far as it goes (the"] [389 1 "// partial chain of a failed X509_verify_cert too), its root included."] [423 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [424 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [425 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [437 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [442 5 "// _servername_callback: the owner died (gh-146080): SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, the callback not called"] [448 5 "// _servername_callback: PyErr_FormatUnraisable, then SSL_AD_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE"] [454 5 "// an integer is the alert's description; anything else SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR, with the unraisable"] [471 3 "// OP_NO_TICKET stops TLS 1.2's tickets only: OpenSSL's TLS 1.3 server then sends stateful tickets, which a"] [472 3 "// client sees as tickets. Go's switch covers both versions, so it follows the version this hello gets."] [504 1 "// ownerOrSelf is the owner (nil once it died), else the socket itself."] [512 1 "// setOwner keeps o (None: none) by a weak reference, as _ssl's owner setter (PyWeakref_NewRef)."] [526 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [527 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [544 3 "// the alert OpenSSL sends for the code (ssl_x509err2alert): Go sends bad_certificate, which the transport"] [545 3 "// rewrites while the alert is in the clear (TLS 1.2; TLS 1.3's is under the handshake keys)"] [556 62 "// a fallback root's constraint"] [560 5 "// Go refuses SHA-1 (and MD5) signatures; OpenSSL refuses them from security level 1 on (63 bits)"] [596 2 "// the security level's checks of X509_verify_cert (check_key_level, check_auth_level): the leaf's key, then"] [597 2 "// each issuer's key and each signature but the trust anchor's"] [612 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [636 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [655 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [656 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [657 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [658 1 "// labels after it."] [694 1 "// sslVerifyAlert is ssl_x509err2alert: the alert for a verification code (certificate_unknown when not listed)."] [698 13 "// unknown_ca"] [700 13 "// bad_certificate"] [702 13 "// certificate_expired"] [704 13 "// certificate_revoked"] [706 13 "// decrypt_error"] [708 13 "// unsupported_certificate"] [710 13 "// internal_error"] [712 12 "// certificate_unknown"] [715 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [717 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [731 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [746 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_erro